.77}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"2a","value":3.5,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"0.9% NaCl","doi":"10.1021/jacs.5c00255","year":2025,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-004006","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"The lipophilicity (logPo/w) was determined by the flask-shaking method and ICP-MS analysis. Equalvolume 0.9% NaCl aqueous (saturated with octanol) was added into a 2 ml saturated stock solution(obtained supernatant by centrifuge) of 1a or 2a in n-octanol (saturated with 0.9% NaCl aqueous), andthe mixture were shaken in the oscillator for 24 h. The mixture was separated to obtain the oil andwater phases. The mixtures were then centrifuged at 5000× g for 5 min. The oil and water phases wereseparated carefully and dried under vacuum. The dried samples were dissolved by HNO3 (65%, 300μL) and diluted to a final volume of 5 mL with Milli-Q water. The Ir(III) concentration (Co or Cw) wasmeasured by ICP-MS using as the internal reference. The Po/w value corresponds to Co/Cw."}],"ccdc":["LUWBEO"]}